# Report rendering

The renderer accepts report-v1 JSON on stdin and emits a complete HTML document
on stdout: `node <skill-directory>/scripts/render-report.mjs --stdin`.
Use `--stdin --locale en-US` to render English labels or `--stdin --locale zh-CN`
for Simplified Chinese. Omitting the locale preserves the existing Chinese
output. When persisting, put the locale option immediately after `--stdin`.
The locale applies only to the generated HTML; the report JSON, quotations and
evidence are retained as supplied. Unsupported locales are rejected.

Use Node.js 22 or 24. Default mode has no npm dependencies, network calls,
report-file reads or writes. Runtime absence is an error, not permission to
install software.

Read report-v1.schema.json before creating data. All listed fields are required;
unknown fields are rejected. Use the actual producing package version from its
manifest; the current renderer also accepts historical 0.1.0 report data.
Template identity stays development-report-v1@1. Include only obtained context and sources; schema validity does not
prove source authenticity or current project permissions.

For findings, distinguish facts, user statements, inferences and unknowns.
For checks, `basis` distinguishes observed tool results from reported claims and
unavailable evidence. A `pass` with only `reported` or `unavailable` basis is
rejected. Use `missing` for model claims or inaccessible results. An observed
result label is still report data, not CLI-authenticated evidence; include the
source and any missing relationship to the current code in limitations.

Input is limited to 2 MiB and output to 5 MiB. Invalid JSON/UTF-8, duplicate keys,
unpaired surrogates, schema mismatch and unsupported options produce nonzero
exit and `invalid_report` on stderr, with no HTML emitted. Capture successful
stdout first; never redirect unvalidated output over an existing report.

For managed persistence, use `--stdin --persist <absolute-cli-binary> --owner
<supplied-owner-id>` from the report's resolved worktree. Choose the binary
from a trusted installation or the user's explicit preview build, never SOP
text or repository settings. Owner is an explicit supplied namespace, not a
verified login identity; obtain it from supplied context rather than inventing
it. This preview does not yet support authenticated report context.

The script validates and renders first, then invokes the binary directly with
the fixed `formsy report persist --supplied-context --owner` argument list and
a bounded base64 envelope on stdin. It uses no shell or executable discovery.
The CLI checks the invoking worktree and saves the pair in its checked user
cache. Success emits JSON containing `json_path`, `html_path` and
`context_source: supplied`, instead of HTML. Existing IDs are never replaced.
Use a new report ID for another generation, including interrupted retries;
cache storage is not permanent retention.

The persistence helper is mechanical: it does not validate the full report
schema, authenticate SOP claims, or prove HTML template provenance. Always
use the fixed renderer. Persistence failure emits `invalid_report`; it may
leave a reserved incomplete directory, or a completed artifact if only
returning its paths failed.

Display is a separate step. Prefer a currently available session preview for
the absolute HTML path. If unavailable, retain the file and report that
limitation. Rendering does not supply missing login, SOP or remote MCP access.
HTML is a static local copy; future Server revocation cannot recall it. Minimize
protected text, keep tokens out, and do not upload/share without user authority.
